msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/help.html:15
msgid ""
"You press \"Get AI suggestions\". The AI reads your title, description, "
"keywords and theme, and the landing page if you have given an address, "
"and suggests better versions. It asks questions about what it cannot "
"know. It takes a few seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/help.html:18
msgid "What happens when you ask for AI suggestions"
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/help.html:20
msgid ""
"If the dataset has a landing page address, the page is downloaded first. "
"The AI uses it as a source of facts for the description. A copy is kept "
"for some hours so that the page is not fetched again for every "
"suggestion, and the panel says how old the copy is. If you know that the "
"page has changed, press \"Download the landing page again\"."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/help.html:21
msgid ""
"The AI analyses the texts. When many people use the assistant at the same"
" time, your request may wait in line; the panel shows your place."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/help.html:22
msgid ""
"The suggestions appear, each next to the current value, with the changes "
"marked in the text. You can edit a suggestion before you use it."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/help.html:23
msgid ""
"You press \"Use suggestion\" for the ones you want. They are put into the"
" form, not saved. Save the dataset as usual."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/help.html:26
msgid "What is sent to the AI service"
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/help.html:27
msgid ""
"Only the title, description, keywords and theme, the landing page address"
" and what was read from that page, the name of your organisation and of "
"the catalogue, the catalogue's guidelines and what the completeness check"
" found. Never data files, resources or personal data. The administrator "
"chooses which AI service is used."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/help.html:29
msgid "Prepared suggestions"
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/help.html:30
msgid ""
"An administrator can have suggestions prepared in advance for many "
"datasets. When you open such a dataset they are shown at once, marked "
"with the time (\"Suggestions prepared 10:45\"), without any waiting. They"
" are valid until the texts change. Press \"Get AI suggestions\" for new "
"ones."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/help.html:32
msgid "Good to know"
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/help.html:34
msgid ""
"The AI can be wrong. Read every suggestion; you are responsible for the "
"metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/help.html:35
msgid ""
"It never decides about confidentiality, personal data, licence or whether"
" data may be published."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/help.html:36
msgid ""
"It does not remove facts from your description, and a suggestion "
"identical to your text is not shown."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/help.html:37
msgid "The name of a place the data is about can be a good keyword."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/help.html:38
msgid ""
"If something fails, the message says what to do. If it does not help, "
"tell an administrator."
msgstr ""

#: ckanext/metadata_assistant/templates/metadata_assistant/translations.html:12
msgid ""
"These are machine translations that nobody has read yet. Compare each one"
" with the source text, correct it if needed, and then apply it. Nothing "
"changes in a dataset until you apply a proposal. You only see the "
"datasets you may edit."
msgstr ""

